  "common_gotchas": [
    "Point SOP changes point-level data; use Primitive SOP when the intended edit is primitive-level.",
    "Edge force only works on primitive face types and its directions are computed in Point SOP, so later transforms do not transform those directions.",
    "Template or second-input values can cycle when point counts differ, which can be useful but can also hide mismatches."
  ],
  "related_snippets": [
    "SOP_snippets"
  ],
  "build_relevance": "point-attribute-editing",
  "last_verified": "2026-06-18",
  "key_concepts": [
    "Point SOP operates on point attributes and complements Primitive SOP, which operates at primitive level.",
    "A second input can provide template values, cycling when it has fewer points than the first input.",
    "Point width and pscale attributes drive later Line MAT, point display, or particle-style sizing workflows.",
    "When attribute logic becomes too conditional, Script SOP is the flexible official escape hatch."
  ]
